          "distinct": true,
          "id": "281eb72337b4a3abe6a601cd75dfad26feff230a",
          "message": "docs(book): single-source guide pages via mdBook {{#include}} anchors (sq-im8u) [OPUS-4.8] (#1184)\n\nMake the existing book/src content pages thin {{#include}} wrappers so their\nprose is build-time-injected from the canonical sources and cannot drift:\n\n- introduction.md  -> README.md `lead` anchor\n- install.md       -> README.md `quickstart-cli` anchor (+ existing sq-384j\n                      {{#rustdoc_include}} of the tested quickstart example)\n- capabilities.md  -> the `scaffold-caveat` anchors in skills/zk-query-proofs/SKILL.md\n                      and skills/mpc/SKILL.md, so the load-bearing ZK/MPC\n                      research-scaffold honesty caveats single-source from their\n                      canonical guides (not-yet-audited / semi-honest hedges intact).\n\nAdd one-per-line ANCHOR/ANCHOR_END markers to README.md + both SKILL.md (a\nmulti-line marker leaks comment lines into the include — caught by `mdbook test`).\n\nExtend the docs.yml path filter to watch the newly-embedded README.md + the two\nSKILL.md so a future anchor rename/removal re-runs the docs lane (self-guarding\nfilter, sq-5f1s4 class — mdBook EXITs 0 on a broken include).\n\nDESIGN JUDGMENT (standing-rule, no greenlight): the capabilities link-TABLE is\ndeliberately NOT single-sourced from the README Features list — the README uses\nrepo-relative skills/ links (required by the lychee internal-links gate) and mdBook\nrewrites them relative to the page mount, so an included copy 404s under Pages. The\ntable keeps mount-portable absolute URLs as a navigation matrix; residual\nsingle-sourcing is tracked as sq-g4h0c.\n\nGates: mdbook 0.4.40 build (no [ERROR]) + mdbook test pass; check-privacy-claims\nclean; markdownlint clean on all changed files.\n\nCo-authored-by: Jesse Wright <jmwright.045@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
          "timestamp": "2026-06-22T20:34:38Z",
          "tree_id": "c8c3c2feec07491f5c3c144fcae6844a0ef4c9e7",
          "url": "https://github.com/jeswr/sparq/commit/281eb72337b4a3abe6a601cd75dfad26feff230a"
